# LeakSanitizer suppressions for G-LSAN-GTK (.port/tools/gates/sanitizers.sh
# --gate lsan-gtk), read AFTER lsan.supp (the lane concatenates the two).
#
# The lane runs one live GTK test (gtk_window_live: a real Window with a core
# Surface, created and closed) under ASan with detect_leaks=1 inside a headless
# sway. Same rules as lsan.supp: every entry is THIRD-PARTY process-lifetime
# state (the GTK/GLib/fontconfig stack below a call we make), each with a row in
# .port/phase-2/SANITIZER_SUPPRESSIONS.md (G ids) giving the reason, the
# evidence and the negative control that keeps a Rust leak RED, and a WHY
# comment directly above it (D6 rule c). A leak in Rustty code is never
# suppressed: it is a finding.
#
# Format: one `leak:<pattern>` per line, as lsan.supp.
